tbeat\",\n            \"description\": \"\\u6bcf5\\u5206\\u949f\\u68c0\\u67e5ECHO\\u534f\\u4f5c\\u5e73\\u53f0\\uff0c\\u53d1\\u73b0\\u65b0\\u6d88\\u606f\\u5219\\u81ea\\u52a8\\u56de\\u5e94\",\n            \"enabled\": true,\n            \"createdAtMs\": 1778862000000,\n            \"schedule\": {\n                \"kind\": \"cron\",\n                \"expr\": \"*/5 * * * *\",\n                \"tz\": \"UTC\"\n            },\n            \"sessionTarget\": \"isolated\",\n            \"wakeMode\": \"now\",\n            \"payload\": {\n                \"kind\": \"agentTurn\",\n                \"message\": \"\\u68c0\\u67e5ECHO Agent\\u534f\\u4f5c\\u5e73\\u53f0\\uff1a\\n1. GET /history?threadId=arbitration&limit=5\\uff08\\u68c0\\u67e5\\u4ef2\\u88c1\\u6a21\\u5757\\u7ebf\\u7a0b\\u6700\\u65b0\\u6d88\\u606f\\uff09\\n2. GET /history?threadId=general&limit=5\\uff08\\u68c0\\u67e5\\u901a\\u7528\\u8ba8\\u8bba\\u7ebf\\u7a0b\\u6700\\u65b0\\u6d88\\u606f\\uff09\\n3. \\u5982\\u679c\\u53d1\\u73b0\\u6709\\u65b0\\u7684\\u8ba8\\u8bba\\uff08\\u4e0d\\u662f\\u6211\\u53d1\\u7684\\uff09\\uff0c\\u9605\\u8bfb\\u5185\\u5bb9\\u5e76\\u7ed9\\u51fa\\u6709\\u4ef7\\u503c\\u7684\\u56de\\u5e94\\n4. \\u7528POST /send\\u53d1\\u6d88\\u606f\\u5230\\u5bf9\\u5e94thread\\n5. API_KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\\n6. base URL: https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev\",\n                \"lightContext\": true\n            },\n            \"delivery\": {\n                \"mode\": \"none\"\n            },\n            \"state\": {}\n        }\n    ]\n}","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-wxlee"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778984516057}}
{"type":"message","id":"4e107e6f","parentId":"588aa875","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:23:03.749Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the full picture! The \"echo-platform-heartbeat\" is a custom cron job that runs every 5 minutes (cron expression `*/5 * * * *`) and checks an ECHO platform API. However, the stuck session in the log was about the Feishu ping being 429'd, which was triggered separately.\n\nBut wait, let me re-read the logs. The log entries I saw were:\n1. `agent:main:cron:echo-platform-heartbeat` state=processing age=152s\n2. HTTP 429 from `open.larksuite.com/open-apis/bot/v1/openclaw_bot/ping`\n\nSo the \"stuck session\" for echo-platform-heartbeat was being reported as a diagnostic warning, but that's likely because the heartbeat cron job was waiting on the Feishu ping to complete (as part of the bot's internal health check).\n\nActually, looking more carefully: the 429 errors from the Feishu ping endpoint are happening separately from the echo-platform-heartbeat cron. The Feishu ping is a built-in health check that the Feishu extension runs (via the `probeFeishu` function). The cron jobs' stuck session warnings might be related to something else.\n\nWait, looking at the log again more carefully:\n```json\n\"stuck session: sessionId=main sessionKey=agent:main:cron:echo-platform-heartbeat state=processing age=152s queueDepth=0\"\n```\n\nThis is saying the cron job is stuck in \"processing\" state. But the echo-platform-heartbeat runs every 5 minutes and seems to complete (state shows \"ok\" and lastDurationMs is 201479ms = ~3.3 minutes).\n\nAnd the 429 error from the probe is happening concurrently - the Feishu extension is calling its built-in probe (ping) every minute as per the gateway health check.\n\nOK so actually there are **three** issues:\n1. **Feishu ping 429** - The built-in Feishu extension's probe is returning 429\n2. **Echo-platform-heartbeat cron running slow** - Takes ~3.3 minutes per run\n3. **Nvidia model 429** - Separate model API rate limiting\n\nBut the user originally said \"飞书通道好像有点哑火了\" meaning the Feishu channel seems quiet/muted. The most direct cause is the Feishu ping getting 429'd, which could cause the channel to appear offline or unresponsive.\n\nNow, the user said \"先1\" meaning go with option 1 from my earlier recommendation. Option 1 was configuring the Feishu channel's ping interval.\n\nBut looking at the code, the probe is **built-in** and not configurable from openclaw.json. The cache TTLs are:\n- SUCCESS: 10 minutes\n- ERROR: 1 minute\n\nSo even if the ping fails, it re-pings after 1 minute. The gateway health check also calls probe every minute.\n\nActually, the issue might be simpler - the Bot API endpoint `/open-apis/bot/v1/openclaw_bot/ping` is a custom bot method, and Lark is rate-limiting it. The probe code doesn't have exponential backoff; it caches the error for only 1 minute and then tries again.\n\nLet me see if there's a way to disable the probe/heartbeat entirely for Feishu, which might be the easiest fix. Or I could modify the probe logic.\n\nActually, I think the most practical fix is:\n1. **Disable the echo-platform-heartbeat cron** (which is the main heartbeat hitting the API) and/or\n2. **Adjust the probe error TTL** to be longer\n\nWait actually - the ping at `open.larksuite.com/open-apis/bot/v1/openclaw_bot/ping` is the Lark Bot's custom method ping. This is used to verify the bot is alive and its credentials work. Getting 429 from this means the tenant/bot has hit its rate limit on the Lark API.\n\nLet me look at what Lark API rate limits exist. Lark (飞书) has tiered rate limits:\n- Free tier: 100 requests per minute\n- Enterprise tier: 500 requests per minute\n- etc.\n\nBut the ping endpoint specifically might have its own limits.\n\nThe practical solution would be to:\n1. Reduce the frequency of the probe\n2. Or disable the probe health check\n\nThe probe cache already helps but the error TTL is only 1 minute. Looking at the code, there's no configurable option exposed. \n\nThe best approach might be to make the probe less aggressive. Let me check if there's a way to disable it or adjust it through configuration.\n\nActually wait - I need to re-examine the log. The log shows the gateway's built-in health check call to probeFeishu() is separate from the user's ECHO platform heartbeat cron. The probe is internal Feishu extension code, not the user's cron job.\n\nLet me check if we can simply stop the ping from happening so often by modifying the probe or adding a config option. But first, let me think about what the user is actually experiencing.\n\nThe user said \"飞书通道好像有点哑火了\" - meaning messages sent through the Feishu channel aren't getting responses or the bot seems unresponsive. This could be because:\n1. The ping is failing, so the gateway considers the channel unhealthy\n2. Or the model API rate limit (nvidia) is causing replies to fail\n\nLooking at the nvidia 429 errors: the model `minimaxai/minimax-m2.7` through nvidia provider is getting rate-limited too. This would cause actual message processing to fail.\n\nSo actually, **both** issues contribute to the bot feeling \"muted\":\n- If the model provider is rate-limited, the agent can't generate responses → messages get no reply\n- If the Feishu ping fails, the channel health check fails\n\nLet me provide the user with actionable steps to fix both issues.\n\nFor option 1 (\"先1\"), the user wants me to adjust the ping/heartbeat frequency. But there's no config option exposed for this in OpenClaw's Feishu extension. The ping interval is hardcoded.\n\nHowever, I can:\n1. Disable the echo-platform-heartbeat cron (user-created, separate issue)\n2. For the Feishu extension probe - it's built-in, can't be easily tuned without code changes\n\nLet me re-examine what the user can actually configure.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"好，主公说先走路径①。我来调低心跳频率。\n\n让我先摸清楚当前心跳配置的可调项：\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_dd87d375e0a44e2bb232e9b1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"heartbeat\\|probe\\|ping\\|healthCheck\\|healthcheck\" /app/dist/runtime-schema-cADw9D2m.js 2>/dev/null | head -20","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778984516060,"responseId":"dea36b22694948398c8ea1d444e372f9"}}
{"type":"message","id":"17030302","parentId":"4e107e6f","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:23:03.779Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_dd87d375e0a44e2bb232e9b1","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"421:\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Controls tagline style in the CLI startup banner: \\\"random\\\" (default) picks from the rotating tagline pool, \\\"default\\\" always shows the neutral default tagline, and \\\"off\\\" hides tagline text while keeping the banner version line.\"\n492:\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Update-channel and startup-check behavior for keeping OpenClaw runtime versions current. Use conservative channels in production and more experimental channels only in controlled environments.\"\n673:\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Named browser profile connection map used for explicit routing to CDP ports or URLs with optional metadata. Keep profile names consistent and avoid overlapping endpoint definitions.\"\n1060:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"When true (default), suppress repeated ACP status/tool projection lines in a turn while keeping raw ACP events unchanged.\"\n2887:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"When true (default), shared image, music, and video generation automatically appends other auth-backed provider defaults after explicit primary/fallback refs. Set false to disable implicit cross-provider fallback while keeping explicit fallbacks.\"\n3689:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Context window size passed to node-llama-cpp when creating the embedding context (default: 4096). 4096 safely covers typical memory-search chunks (128–512 tokens) while keeping non-weight VRAM bounded. Lower to 1024–2048 on resource-constrained hosts. Set to \\\"auto\\\" to let node-llama-cpp use the model's trained maximum — not recommended for large models (e.g. Qwen3-Embedding-8B trained on 40 960 tokens can push VRAM from ~8.8 GB to ~32 GB).\"\n4222:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Embedded Pi execution contract: \\\"default\\\" keeps the standard runner behavior, while \\\"strict-agentic\\\" keeps OpenAI/OpenAI Codex GPT-5-family runs acting until they hit a real blocker instead of stopping at plans or filler.\"\n4414:\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttypingIntervalSeconds: {\n4419:\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttypingMode: { anyOf: [\n4437:\t\t\t\t\t\t\theartbeat: {\n4463:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Controls whether heartbeat delivery may target direct/DM chats: \\\"allow\\\" (default) permits DM delivery and \\\"block\\\" suppresses direct-target sends.\"\n4471:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Includes the default agent's ## Heartbeats system prompt section when true. Turn this off to keep heartbeat runtime behavior while omitting the heartbeat prompt instructions from the agent system prompt.\"\n4481:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Suppress tool error warning payloads during heartbeat runs.\"\n4488:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Maximum time in seconds allowed for a heartbeat agent turn before it is aborted. Leave unset to use agents.defaults.timeoutSeconds.\"\n5505:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\theartbeat: {\n5531:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Per-agent override for heartbeat direct/DM delivery policy; use \\\"block\\\" for agents that should only send heartbeat alerts to non-DM destinations.\"\n5539:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Per-agent override for whether the default agent's ## Heartbeats system prompt section is injected. Use false to keep heartbeat runtime behavior but omit the heartbeat prompt instructions from that agent's system prompt.\"\n5549:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Suppress tool error warning payloads during heartbeat runs.\"\n5556:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Per-agent maximum time in seconds allowed for a heartbeat agent turn before it is aborted. Leave unset to inherit the merged heartbeat/default agent timeout.\"\n6311:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tpingPong: { type: \"boolean\" }"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":24,"aggregated":"421:\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Controls tagline style in the CLI startup banner: \\\"random\\\" (default) picks from the rotating tagline pool, \\\"default\\\" always shows the neutral default tagline, and \\\"off\\\" hides tagline text while keeping the banner version line.\"\n492:\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Update-channel and startup-check behavior for keeping OpenClaw runtime versions current. Use conservative channels in production and more experimental channels only in controlled environments.\"\n673:\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Named browser profile connection map used for explicit routing to CDP ports or URLs with optional metadata. Keep profile names consistent and avoid overlapping endpoint definitions.\"\n1060:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"When true (default), suppress repeated ACP status/tool projection lines in a turn while keeping raw ACP events unchanged.\"\n2887:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"When true (default), shared image, music, and video generation automatically appends other auth-backed provider defaults after explicit primary/fallback refs. Set false to disable implicit cross-provider fallback while keeping explicit fallbacks.\"\n3689:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Context window size passed to node-llama-cpp when creating the embedding context (default: 4096). 4096 safely covers typical memory-search chunks (128–512 tokens) while keeping non-weight VRAM bounded. Lower to 1024–2048 on resource-constrained hosts. Set to \\\"auto\\\" to let node-llama-cpp use the model's trained maximum — not recommended for large models (e.g. Qwen3-Embedding-8B trained on 40 960 tokens can push VRAM from ~8.8 GB to ~32 GB).\"\n4222:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Embedded Pi execution contract: \\\"default\\\" keeps the standard runner behavior, while \\\"strict-agentic\\\" keeps OpenAI/OpenAI Codex GPT-5-family runs acting until they hit a real blocker instead of stopping at plans or filler.\"\n4414:\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttypingIntervalSeconds: {\n4419:\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttypingMode: { anyOf: [\n4437:\t\t\t\t\t\t\theartbeat: {\n4463:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Controls whether heartbeat delivery may target direct/DM chats: \\\"allow\\\" (default) permits DM delivery and \\\"block\\\" suppresses direct-target sends.\"\n4471:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Includes the default agent's ## Heartbeats system prompt section when true. Turn this off to keep heartbeat runtime behavior while omitting the heartbeat prompt instructions from the agent system prompt.\"\n4481:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Suppress tool error warning payloads during heartbeat runs.\"\n4488:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Maximum time in seconds allowed for a heartbeat agent turn before it is aborted. Leave unset to use agents.defaults.timeoutSeconds.\"\n5505:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\theartbeat: {\n5531:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Per-agent override for heartbeat direct/DM delivery policy; use \\\"block\\\" for agents that should only send heartbeat alerts to non-DM destinations.\"\n5539:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Per-agent override for whether the default agent's ## Heartbeats system prompt section is injected. Use false to keep heartbeat runtime behavior but omit the heartbeat prompt instructions from that agent's system prompt.\"\n5549:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Suppress tool error warning payloads during heartbeat runs.\"\n5556:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdescription: \"Per-agent maximum time in seconds allowed for a heartbeat agent turn before it is aborted. Leave unset to inherit the merged heartbeat/default agent timeout.\"\n6311:\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tpingPong: { type: \"boolean\" }","cwd":"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-wxlee"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1778984583779}}
