{"type":"message","id":"936b7cbe","parentId":"b749019d","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:25:00.808Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so the probe is only called during channel status checks, not periodically from the gateway. The actual 429 errors were from the gateway's own health check pinging the endpoint.\n\nNow let me also look at how the \"echo-platform-heartbeat\" cron is connected to the Feishu 429 issue. Looking at the jobs-state.json:\n\n```json\n\"echo-platform-heartbeat\": {\n  \"lastRunStatus\": \"ok\",\n  \"lastDurationMs\": 201479,  // ~3.3 minutes\n  \"runningAtMs\": 1778984400006  // currently running\n}\n```\n\nThe echo-platform-heartbeat runs every 5 minutes and each run takes ~3.3 minutes. It's doing HTTP calls to the ECHO platform. This is a separate issue from the Feishu ping 429.\n\nBut looking at the logs more carefully, the 429 errors from Feishu ping are coming from the gateway health check. The gateway appears to be pinging each Feishu account's bot endpoint at regular intervals.\n\nLet me check how the gateway does health checks.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c13212dbba5e4950b3c8afc2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"FEISHU_PROBE\\|probeFeishu\\|healthCheck\\|health\\.check\\|statusLines\\|resolveStatus\" /app/dist/extensions/feishu/channel-BrSg_Wfu.js 2>/dev/null | head -20","timeout":10}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8f67720be268455d98b42c62","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"healthCheck\\|status\\|probe\" /app/dist/subsystem-CWI_MDy_.js 2>/dev/null | head -20","timeout":10}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778984640751,"responseId":"dc6cf07bd2c04c9d8d9e92c2aa3bab1f"}}
